---
import Default from "../layouts/Default.astro";
const lastUpdated = "April 26, 2026";
---

<Default
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms of service for Alvey Tools products and the marketing site at alveyautomation.com/tools."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 prose-tools">
    <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-amber-400 font-semibold mb-3">
      Legal
    </div>
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl text-ink-100 mb-3">
      Terms of Service
    </h1>
    <p class="text-ink-400 text-sm mb-10">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      These terms govern your use of products listed at
      <a href="/" class="text-amber-400 hover:underline">alveyautomation.com/tools</a>
      ("Alvey Tools") and any download, marketplace install, or open-source
      package linked from this site. By using a product you agree to these
      terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Alvey Tools is a sub-brand of Alvey Automation, operated by Brett
      Alvey. Contact: <code>brett@alveyautomation.com</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>License</h2>
    <p>
      Open-source MCP servers and the runnable code shipped with paid
      downloads are MIT-licensed unless explicitly noted otherwise. You may
      use them in commercial projects, modify them, and redistribute them
      subject to the MIT terms.
    </p>
    <p>
      The PDF documentation included with the methodology pack is licensed
      for the purchaser's individual use. Please don't redistribute the PDF.
    </p>

    <h2>Subscription apps</h2>
    <p>
      Marketplace apps (QuickBooks, Shopify, Stripe) are billed on a monthly
      recurring basis through the respective marketplace's billing system.
      You can cancel at any time from the marketplace's app management UI.
      Cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing period.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not pro-rate refunds for partial months on subscription apps,
      but if a subscription app fails to deliver value in your first 30 days
      we'll refund your most recent charge, email
      <code>brett@alveyautomation.com</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>One-time downloads</h2>
    <p>
      Refund windows for one-time downloads vary by product:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Methodology Pack ($149)</strong>. 14-day refund window.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Security Stack ($49)</strong>. 30-day refund window.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Flask Scaffold ($79)</strong>. 7-day refund window.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Email <code>brett@alveyautomation.com</code> within the relevant
      window for a no-friction refund. Refunds are processed through Gumroad
      and typically appear within 3-5 business days.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      All products are provided "as is" without warranty of any kind. While
      every product on this site has been tested in production, you are
      responsible for evaluating fitness for your own use case before
      relying on a product for business-critical work.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, Alvey Automation's total
      liability arising out of or related to your use of any product is
      limited to the amount you paid for that product in the prior 12
      months. We are not liable for indirect, incidental, special,
      consequential, or punitive damages.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Don't use these products to break the law, harm others, or infringe
      anyone's rights. Don't attempt to circumvent security controls on the
      hosted apps. Don't redistribute the PDF documentation. Don't impersonate
      Alvey Automation in derivative work.
    </p>

    <h2>Termination</h2>
    <p>
      We may terminate access to subscription apps if you violate these
      terms. We will not retroactively revoke MIT-licensed downloads, once
      you have a copy under MIT, that license stands.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms as products evolve. Material changes will
      be announced via product update emails to existing customers. Your
      continued use of a product after changes constitutes acceptance.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms: <code>brett@alveyautomation.com</code>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Default>
